# Merge policy for pool/* -> dev. Committed with the repo, one key=value per
# line. Change it with bin/set-merge-policy (admin-gated, logs a [MODE]
# commit). Read by bin/finalize-pool-merge (off-grid), bin/init-pool-merge
# (connected) and the pre-push hook. dev -> main rules are never affected.
#
# dev_merge_who       anyone | admins | list
#                     Who may merge a pool into dev. admins = emails listed
#                     in admins.txt (no admins.txt = permissive first run);
#                     list = emails in dev_merge_list.
# dev_merge_list      Comma-separated emails, used when dev_merge_who=list.
# dev_merge_pr        required | optional
#                     required: in connected mode a pool reaches dev only
#                     through a PR; pre-push refuses a local merge push to dev.
# dev_merge_approval  none | required
#                     required: the pool -> dev merge commit carries an
#                     "Approved-by: <email>" trailer naming an allowed merger
#                     other than the operator.
# dev_merge_gates     Comma-separated ci-local check names (push trigger) that
#                     must pass before the close-up, e.g. required.compile.
# dev_merge_max_commits Most non-merge commits one pool may bring into dev
#                     (default 20, 0 = no cap). Bigger deliveries land as
#                     sequential pools. Never lifted by warp.
#
# bin/warp on lifts who, pr and approval for pool -> dev only; gates and the
# commit cap still run.
dev_merge_who=admins
dev_merge_list=
dev_merge_pr=required
dev_merge_approval=none
dev_merge_gates=
dev_merge_max_commits=20
